The '''2026 Los Angeles Dodgers season''' was the 137th season for the [[Los Angeles Dodgers]] franchise in [[Major League Baseball]] (MLB), their 69th season in [[Los Angeles]], [[California]], and their 65th season playing home games at [[Dodger Stadium]]. They entered the season as the two-time defending [[National League (baseball)|National League]] champions, and two-time defending [[World Series]] champions. They failed to become the first team to [[three-peat]] since the [[2000 New York Yankees season|2000 New York Yankees]], as well as the first National League team to accomplish this feat. This was the Dodgers first season since [[2007 Los Angeles Dodgers season|2007]] to not include pitcher [[Clayton Kershaw]] on the active roster, as he retired after the [[2025 Los Angeles Dodgers season|2025 season]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Simon |first=Andrew |date=December 14, 2025 |title=Meet the Dodgers' Kershaw Era All-Star squad |url=https://www.mlb.com/news/dodgers-kershaw-era-all-star-team-picks |access-date=September 17, 2026 |website=MLB.com}}</ref> This was the last season for utilityman and 2025 World Series hero, [[Miguel Rojas (baseball)|Miguel Rojas]], who will join the front office after the season.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Macofsky |first=Jacob |date=2025-12-05 |title=Dodgers notes: Miguel Rojas, Teoscar Hernández, Fernando Valenzuela |url=https://www.truebluela.com/dodgers-links/108156/dodgers-miguel-rojas-teoscar-hernandez-fernando-valenzuela-robert-suarez-pete-fairbanks |access-date=2026-04-28 |website=True Blue LA |language=en-US}}</ref>

With their 14th consecutive postseason appearance, the Dodgers matched the 1991–2005 [[Atlanta Braves]] for the longest consecutive postseason streak in MLB history. They clinched their 13th [[National League West]] title in 14 seasons (fifth consecutive) on September 17 with a road victory over the [[2026 Cincinnati Reds season|Cincinnati Reds]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Chen |first=Sonja |date=September 17, 2026 |title=Tucker's near-cycle clinches LA's 5th straight NL West title, 13th in 14 years |url=https://www.mlb.com/news/dodgers-clinch-2026-nl-west-title |access-date= |website=MLB.com}}</ref> With a September 27 road win against the [[2026 San Francisco Giants season|San Francisco Giants]], they finished with [[List of Major League Baseball 100 win seasons|100 wins]] for the sixth time in the last ten seasons. They defeated the [[2026 Atlanta Braves season|Atlanta Braves]] in the [[2026 National League Division Series|National League Division Series]] in four games and advanced to the [[2026 National League Championship Series|National League Championship Series]] for the third year in a row, where they were swept by the eventual [[2026 World Series|World Series]] champion [[2026 Milwaukee Brewers season|Milwaukee Brewers]] in four games, ending their hopes of three-peating the World Series.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Dodgers' dream of a World Series three-peat ends as Brewers complete NLCS sweep|url=https://abc7.com/post/dodgers-dream-world-series-peat-ends-brewers-complete-nlcs-sweep/19942576/|date=October 16, 2026|website=ABC 7 Los Angeles}}</ref>

==Offseason==
===Stadium naming rights deal===
During the off-season the Dodgers struck a five-year / $125 million+ deal <ref>{{Cite news |last=Blum |first=Sam |date=2026-04-09 |title=Uniqlo Field at Dodger Stadium? To some Dodgers fans, that's a case of mistaken identity |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7181269/2026/04/09/uniqlo-field-dodger-stadium-mlb-naming-rights/ |access-date=2026-04-21 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> with Japanese designer and retailer [[Uniqlo]] to rename the playing field at [[Dodger Stadium]] to "Uniqlo Field at Dodger Stadium".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.latimes.com/sports/dodgers/story/2026-03-26/dodger-stadium-uniqlo-field-naming-rights|title=The signs say Uniqlo Field. You will continue to say Dodger Stadium|work=Los Angeles Times|first=Bill|last=Shaikin|date=March 26, 2026|access-date=March 26, 2026}}</ref>

===Front office===
On December 3, the Dodgers Senior Vice-President of Baseball Operations [[Josh Byrnes]] left the team to become the [[General manager (baseball)|General Manager]] of the [[Colorado Rockies]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.truebluela.com/los-angeles-dodgers-news-notes/108091/rockies-josh-byrnes-general-manager-dodgers|title=Rockies hire Dodgers exec Josh Byrnes as general manager|first=Eric|last=Stephen|work=SB Nation|date=December 3, 2025|access-date=December 3, 2025}}</ref>

===Roster departures===
Pitcher [[Clayton Kershaw]], who spent his entire 18-season career with the Dodgers, announced his retirement in September.<ref name=Kershaw>{{cite news |title=Clayton Kershaw goes out on top with third Dodgers World Series title: 'How can I script it any better?' |first=Matt |last=Snyder |work=[[CBS Sports]] |date=November 1, 2025 |access-date=November 2, 2025 |url=https://www.cbssports.com/mlb/news/clayton-kershaw-world-series-dodgers-retirement/}}</ref>

On November 2, 2025, the day after the conclusion of the [[2025 World Series]], six Dodgers players became free agents. This included pitchers [[Andrew Heaney]], [[Michael Kopech]], and [[Kirby Yates]], infielder [[Miguel Rojas (baseball)|Miguel Rojas]], outfielder [[Michael Conforto]], and utility player [[Enrique Hernández (baseball)|Kiké Hernández]].<ref name=FreeAgents>{{cite news |title=Clayton Kershaw, Kiké Hernández among 7 Dodgers free agents|first=Eric |last=Stephen |work=SB Nation |date=November 2, 2025 |access-date=November 2, 2025 |url=https://www.truebluela.com/dodgers-roster/106387/dodgers-free-agents-clayton-kershaw-enrique-hernandez}}</ref> On November 6, the Dodgers designated pitcher [[Tony Gonsolin]] for assignment and outrighted pitcher [[Michael Grove]] and outfielder [[Justin Dean]].<ref name=gonsolin>{{cite web|url=https://www.mlbtraderumors.com/2025/11/dodgers-designate-tony-gonsolin-for-assignment.html|title=Dodgers Designate Tony Gonsolin For Assignment|work=MLB Trade Rumors|first=Darragh|last=McDonald|date=November 6, 2025|access-date=November 6, 2025}}</ref> On November 12, catcher [[Ben Rortvedt]] was claimed off waivers by the [[Cincinnati Reds]].<ref name=rort>{{cite web|url=https://www.mlbtraderumors.com/2025/11/reds-claim-ben-rortvedt.html|title=Reds Claim Ben Rortvedt|work=MLB Trade Rumors|first=Darragh|last=McDonald|date=November 12, 2025|access-date=November 12, 2025}}</ref> On November 21, the Dodgers non-tendered pitchers [[Nick Frasso]] and [[Evan Phillips]], making them free agents.<ref name=nontenders>{{cite web|url=https://www.latimes.com/sports/dodgers/story/2025-11-21/dodgers-non-tender-reliever-evan-phillips|title=Dodgers non-tender Evan Phillips, but remain interested in re-signing the reliever|work=Los Angeles Times|first=Jack|last=Harris|date=November 21, 2025|access-date=November 21, 2025}}</ref> On December 29, they traded outfielder [[Esteury Ruiz]] to the [[Miami Marlins]] in exchange for minor leaguer Adriano Marrero.<ref name=ruiz>{{cite web|url=https://www.mlbtraderumors.com/2025/12/dodgers-to-trade-esteury-ruiz-to-marlins.html|title=Dodgers Trade Esteury Ruiz To Marlins|work=MLB Trade Rumors|first=Anthony|last=Franco|date=December 29, 2025|access-date=December 30, 2025}}</ref> On February 6, the Dodgers designated pitcher [[Anthony Banda]] for assignment.<ref name=Banda>{{Cite web|url=https://www.mlbtraderumors.com/2026/02/dodgers-designate-anthony-banda-for-assignment.html|title=Dodgers Designate Anthony Banda For Assignment|first=Darragh|last=McDonald|date=February 6, 2026|work=MLB Trade Rumors}}</ref>

===Roster additions===
On November 6, 2025, the Dodgers selected the contracts of outfielder / first baseman [[Ryan Ward (baseball)|Ryan Ward]] and pitcher [[Robinson Ortiz]] and added them to the 40-man roster<ref name=ward>{{cite web|url=https://www.mlbtraderumors.com/2025/11/dodgers-exercise-club-option-on-max-muncy.html|title=Dodgers Exercise Club Options On Max Muncy, Alex Vesia|work=MLB Trade Rumors|first=Darragh|last=McDonald|date=November 6, 2025|access-date=November 6, 2025}}</ref><ref name=gonsolin/> Ortiz was traded to the [[Seattle Mariners]] on November 16.<ref name=ortiz>{{cite web|url=https://www.truebluela.com/dodgers-roster/107604/dodgers-trade-robinson-ortiz-tyler-gough-mariners|title=Dodgers trade Robinson Ortiz to Mariners for Tyler Gough|work=SB Nation|date=November 17, 2025|first=Eric|last=Stephen|access-date=November 17, 2025}}</ref> Pitcher [[Ronan Kopp]] was added to the 40-man roster on November 18.<ref name=kopp>{{cite web|url=https://www.truebluela.com/dodgers-roster/107660/dodgers-40-man-roster-ronan-kopp|title=Dodgers add Ronan Kopp to 40-man roster|work=SB Nation|first=Eric|last=Stephen|date=November 18, 2025|access-date=November 18, 2025}}</ref> On December 5, the Dodgers announced that they had re-signed infielder [[Miguel Rojas (baseball)|Miguel Rojas]] on a one-year, $5.5 million contract.<ref name=rojas>{{cite web|url=https://www.mlb.com/dodgers/news/miguel-rojas-dodgers-free-agent-contract|title=World Series hero Rojas rejoins Dodgers on 1-year, $5.5 million deal|work=mlb.com|first=Sonja|last=Chen|date=December 4, 2025|access-date=December 5, 2025}}</ref> On December 12, they claimed outfielder [[Mike Siani (baseball)|Mike Siani]] off waivers from the [[Atlanta Braves]].<ref name=siani>{{cite web|url=https://www.mlbtraderumors.com/2025/12/dodgers-claim-michael-siani.html|title=Dodgers Claim Michael Siani|work=mlb trade rumors|first=Darragh|last=McDonald|date=December 12, 2025|access-date=December 12, 2025}}</ref> The same day, they signed relief pitcher [[Edwin Díaz]] to a three-year, $69 million contract.<ref name=diaz>{{cite web|url=https://www.mlb.com/dodgers/news/edwin-diaz-dodgers-contract|title=Dodgers reach 3-year deal with standout closer Díaz|work=mlb.com|first=Sonja and David Adler|last=Chen|date=December 12, 2025|accessdate=December 12, 2025}}</ref> On January 9, they claimed infielder [[Ryan Fitzgerald (baseball)|Ryan Fitzgerald]] off waivers from the [[Minnesota Twins]].<ref name=ryanfitz>{{cite web|url=https://www.mlbtraderumors.com/2026/01/dodgers-claim-ryan-fitzgerald.html|title=Dodgers Claim Ryan Fitzgerald|work=MLB Trade Rumors|first=Darragh|last=McDonald|date=January 9, 2026|access-date=January 9, 2026}}</ref> On January 13, they designated Fitzgerald for assignment and signed infielder [[Andy Ibáñez]] to a one-year, $1.2 million contract.<ref name=ibanez>{{cite web|url=https://www.truebluela.com/dodgers-roster/109001/dodgers-andy-ibanez-ryan-fitzgerald|title=Dodgers finalize Andy Ibáñez contract, DFA newcomer Ryan Fitzgerald|work=SB Nation|first=Eric|last=Stephen|date=January 13, 2026|access-date=January 14, 2026}}</ref> On January 21, they designated Siani for assignment<ref name=sianidfa>{{cite web|url=https://www.mlbtraderumors.com/2026/01/dodgers-designate-michael-siani-for-assignment.html|title=Dodgers Designate Michael Siani For Assignment|work=MLB Trade Rumors|first=Steve|last=Adams|date=January 21, 2026|access-date=January 21, 2026}}</ref> and signed outfielder [[Kyle Tucker]] to a four-year, $240 million contract.<ref name=tucker>{{cite web|url=https://www.mlb.com/dodgers/news/kyle-tucker-dodgers-contract|title=Tucker picks Dodgers, agrees to four-year contract|work=mlb.com|first=Sonja|last=Chen|date=January 21, 2026|access-date=January 21, 2026}}</ref> On February 3, they re-claimed Siani off waivers (from the [[New York Yankees]]) and designated Ibáñez for assignment.<ref name=siani-ibanez>{{Cite web|url=https://www.mlbtraderumors.com/2026/02/dodgers-claim-michael-siani-waivers-dfa-andy-ibanez.html|title=Dodgers Claim Michael Siani, DFA Andy Ibanez|first=Steve|last=Adams|date=February 3, 2026|website=MLB Trade Rumors}}</ref> Pitcher [[Evan Phillips]] was re-signed for one year and $6.5 million, on February 11.<ref name=Phillips>{{Cite web|url=https://www.mlbtraderumors.com/2026/02/dodgers-re-sign-evan-phillips-dfa-ben-rortvedt.html|title=Dodgers Re-Sign Evan Phillips, Designate Ben Rortvedt|first=Steve|last=Adams|date=February 11, 2026|website=MLB Trade Rumors}}</ref> The following day, they re-signed utility player [[Enrique Hernández (baseball)|Kiké Hernández]] to a one year, $4.5 million contract.<ref name=Kiké>{{Cite web|title=Dodgers Re-Sign Kiké Hernández|url=https://www.mlbtraderumors.com/2026/02/dodgers-to-re-sign-kike-hernandez.html|access-date=February 12, 2026|website=mlbtraderumors.com|language=en}}</ref>  Outfielder [[Jack Suwinski]] was claimed off waivers from the [[Pittsburgh Pirates]] on February 22.<ref name=Suwin>{{cite web|url=https://www.mlbtraderumors.com/2026/02/dodgers-to-claim-jack-suwinski.html|title=Dodgers Claim Jack Suwinski|work=MLB Trade Rumors|first=Charlie|last=Wright|date=February 21, 2026|access-date=February 22, 2026}}</ref>

