The Dodgers began [[spring training]] on February 13, 2026 at [[Camelback Ranch]] in [[Glendale, Arizona]], with the first [[Cactus League]] game on February 21. While at Camelback Ranch, the Dodgers also played an exhibition game on March 4 against the [[Mexico national baseball team]] as part of promotion for the [[2026 World Baseball Classic]].<ref>{{cite news |title=World Baseball Classic exhibitions highlight 2026 Spring Training schedule |first=Paul |last=Casella |work=[[MLB.com]] |date=November 5, 2025 |access-date=November 6, 2025 |url=https://www.mlb.com/news/mlb-2026-spring-training-schedule}}</ref> They also played in three [[Freeway Series]] exhibition games against the [[Los Angeles Angels]] before beginning the regular season on March 26.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.si.com/mlb/angels/onsi/what-we-learned-from-the-freeway-series-finale-01kmhkf4dxfs|title=What We Learned from the Freeway Series Finale|magazine=Sports Illustrated|first=Jeff|last=Joiner|date=March 25, 2026|access-date=March 26, 2026}}</ref> On March 19, the Dodgers selected the contract of utility player [[Santiago Espinal]] and added him to the major league roster.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.truebluela.com/dodgers-roster/111580/santiago-espinal-opening-day-roster|title=Dodgers add Santiago Espinal to roster|work=SB Nation|first=Eric|last=Stephen|date=March 18, 2026|access-date=March 19, 2026}}</ref>

===World Baseball Classic===
{{Main|2026 World Baseball Classic}}

Nine Dodgers players were chosen to represent countries during the World Baseball Classic. [[Shohei Ohtani]] and [[Yoshinobu Yamamoto]] for [[Japan national baseball team|Japan]], [[Will Smith (catcher)|Will Smith]] and recently retired [[Clayton Kershaw]] for [[United States national baseball team|Team USA]], [[Edwin Díaz]] for [[Puerto Rico national baseball team|Puerto Rico]], [[Hyeseong Kim]] for [[South Korea national baseball team|Korea]], Antonio Knowles for [[Great Britain national baseball team|Great Britain]], [[Jake Gelof]] for [[Israel national baseball team|Israel]] and Shawndrick Oduber for [[Netherlands national baseball team|Netherlands]]. In addition several members of the Dodgers organization were listed as coaches for the tournament including [[Dino Ebel]] (USA), Jair Fernandez ([[Colombia national baseball team|Colombia]]), [[Blake Gailen]] (Israel), [[Plácido Polanco]] and [[Joel Peralta]] ([[Dominican Republic national baseball team|Dominican Republic]]).<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.truebluela.com/world-baseball-classic/109383/dodgers-world-baseball-classic-rosters|title=Dodgers on 2026 World Baseball Classic rosters|work=SB Nation|first=Eric|last=Stephen|date=February 5, 2026|access-date=February 6, 2026}}</ref>

